ar","forms":[["I / you / we / they put","Put the paper on the desk."],["he / she / it puts","Ponha o papel na mesa."]]}]},{"type":"table","head":["Phrasal verb","Significado","Exemplo"],"rows":[["**put forward**","propor","She put forward a plan. — Ela propôs um plano."],["**put off**","adiar","They put off the vote. — Eles adiaram a votação."]],"cap":"Phrasal verbs"}]},{"tag":"Escuta e diálogo","title":"Office","blocks":[{"type":"dialog","title":"Office","lines":[["Ana","Can we put off the vote?","Podemos adiar a votação?"],["Leo","Why? We can’t put up with more delays.","Por quê? Não toleramos mais atrasos."],["Ana","I want to put forward a better plan.","Quero propor um plano melhor."],["Leo","Fine. Put it in the shared folder.","Certo. Coloque na pasta compartilhada."]]},{"type":"pron","title":"Pronúncia: Acento para enfatizar informação","items":[{"label":"Acento para enfatizar informação","note":"A palavra nova ou importante recebe o acento mais forte: I want the RED one, not the blue one.","words":["I want the RED one.","She said TUESDAY.","Not TWO, THREE.","He BOUGHT it."]}]}]},{"tag":"Fala","title":"Speaking","blocks":[{"type":"speak","title":"Speaking","prompts":[{"q":"Use put forward.","pt":"Use.","model":"I’d like to put forward an idea."},{"q":"Use put off.","pt":"Use.","model":"We put off the meeting."},{"q":"Use put up with.","pt":"Use.","model":"I can’t put up with the noise."}]}]},{"tag":"Escrita","title":"Writing","blocks":[{"type":"write","task":"Write 5 sentences with put in different meanings.","model":"I put forward a proposal. We put off the vote. I can’t put up with delays. Please put on your calendar the new date. We will put a clear agenda in place.","checklist":["Usei **put**","Usei **4 sentidos**","5 frases"],"words":"5 frases"}]},{"tag":"Revisão e exame","title":"Review · Exam strategy · Teacher’s note","blocks":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Check yourself","items":[{"q":"What does “shared drive” mean?","opts":["proposta preliminar","unidade c